[statement]
A provider's priority (`k:`) is read as a number that saturates at 2^64 - 1 before it is kept modulo 2^16, so a number past that is 65535: `p1` at `k:18446744073709551616` against `p2` at `k:65534`.

[repository]
P:p1
V:1.0-r0
p:v
k:18446744073709551616

P:p2
V:1.0-r0
p:v
k:65534

[request]
v

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install p1 1.0-r0
